  "notes": "Skift body is paywalled after two paragraphs; Q3 revenue, segment growth and fuel bill come from Skift's Key Points/Summary block and match United's own press release (SEC 8-K Exhibit 99.1, 2026-10-20) and its Investor Update (Exhibit 99.2). Investing.com via Yahoo (2026-10-21) also matches revenue, segments, 49.5 million customers and the $0.50-$1.50 range. Analyst consensus EPS left out: Skift says $1.76, Investing.com says $1.88. Per-gallon prices left out (word out of level); only the $0.45 gap and its ~$1/share effect are used. Fare and capacity remarks by the CFO and Delta's guidance cut appear only in Skift's AI summary, not used.",
  "figures": [
   {
    "id": "f1",
    "text": "on Tuesday United issued a disappointing fourth-quarter earnings outlook due to high jet fuel costs",
    "quote": "United Airlines on Tuesday issued a disappointing earnings outlook for the fourth quarter due to continued high costs for jet fuel."
   },
   {
    "id": "f2",
    "text": "results released October 20, 2026",
    "quote": "CHICAGO, October 20, 2026"
   },
   {
    "id": "f3",
    "text": "Q3 2026 revenue $17.9 billion, up 17% from Q3 2025, a record",
    "quote": "Q3 total operating revenue of $17.9 billion rose 17% year-over-year and set an all-time record"
   },
   {
    "id": "f4",
    "text": "record 49.5 million customers in Q3",
    "quote": "United carried a record 49.5 million customers during Q3"
   },
   {
    "id": "f5",
    "text": "vs Q3 2025: premium up 17%, basic economy up 16%, loyalty up 17%, cargo up 23%",
    "quote": "compared to the third quarter of 2025, Premium revenue was up 17%, revenue from Basic Economy was up 16%, loyalty revenue was up 17% and cargo revenue was up 23%."
   },
   {
    "id": "f6",
    "text": "fuel expense up 62% vs Q3 2025",
    "quote": "within guidance despite a 62% increase in fuel expense"
   },
   {
    "id": "f7",
    "text": "fuel expense up $1.8 billion vs Q3 2025",
    "quote": "Fuel expense was up $1.8 billion compared to third-quarter 2025 as jet fuel prices remained volatile."
   },
   {
    "id": "f8",
    "text": "Q4 adjusted EPS $0.50 to $1.50 (50 cents to $1.50), short of analyst expectations",
    "quote": "It now expects adjusted earnings per share to range from $0.50 to $1.50, short of the $1.76 analysts expected."
   },
   {
    "id": "f9",
    "text": "fuel assumption about $0.45 (45 cents) higher than consensus, worth about $1 a share",
    "quote": "about $0.45 higher than what consensus assumed, a difference it said is worth roughly $1 a share."
   },
   {
    "id": "f10",
    "text": "Q4 revenue growth over 20% year over year, another record",
    "quote": "United expects Q4 total operating revenue growth to accelerate versus Q3 and set another record with an over 20% year-over-year increase"
   },
   {
    "id": "f11",
    "text": "despite fuel costs, demand is high; premium and loyalty up 17%",
    "quote": "Despite the higher fuel costs, United is still seeing high travel demand — premium and loyalty revenues were both up 17%."
   }
  ]
